          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C8\") (value \"1mF/25V\") (footprint \"Capacitor_SMD:C_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.18x1.45mm_HandSolder\") ...)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The EPD boost/charge-pump reservoir capacitance is 1000x too large and physically impossible in an 0805 package; this would alter EPD power-up, boost timing, and likely prevent correct display operation.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U5"],
      "pins": ["U5.13", "U5.14"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "U5 pins 13 and 14 (LAN_PORT3_TX+ and LAN_PORT3_TX-) are both connected to the GND net.",
      "expected": "These Ethernet PHY differential outputs should not be tied directly to ground; they should be either left unconnected or used as intended GPIO/Ethernet signals.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX+\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"14\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX-\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "the RJ45 jack J5's data pads ... all appear in the netlist as individually unconnected ... while the LAN1_RX+/- ... resolve to single-node nets containing only U5 pins."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Shorting the Ethernet PHY transmit pair to ground can cause excessive current, heating, or damage if the PHY is enabled, and corrupts the Ethernet interface.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["Display_Power_Switch", "GND"],
      "observed": "C1 is populated as 0.1uF/16V.",
      "expected": "C1 should be 1uF/25V according to the EPD reference circuit specification.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V | Matches default"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C1\") (value \"0.1uF/16V\") (footprint \"Capacitor_SMD:C_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.18x1.45mm_HandSolder\") ...)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The EPD VDD/VDDIO rail has 10x less decoupling than intended, which may reduce display stability or cause marginal operation.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple anomalies, most notably C8 being 1mF instead of 1uF and U5 Ethernet transmit pins shorted to ground. C1 is also 0.1uF instead of the specified 1uF."
}

